/ so it is ungated by any AC","L103/L111 fake_convert literals are hermetic (both sides 3.6.1) but become stale/misleading after the bump"],"finding":"The plan's pin-provenance inventory omits tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py, a consumer of the changed generator.LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION constant that hard-codes '3.6.1' and will FAIL after the step-4a bump. At L190-195 and L243-249 it builds provenance with version=generator.LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION (which step 4a changes to the new bundled version) but calls validate_pandoc_provenance(..., version=\"3.6.1\", ...); the version-match check then raises 'Pandoc version mismatch'. Because this file lives under tests/scripts/ (not tests/unit/), neither AC5's `pytest tests/unit` nor step 7's verify set exercises it, so the breakage is silent within the plan's gates.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa8800a681952db1c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Step 3 grep inventory / Scope 'Pin-provenance consumers' / AC3/AC5","norm_id":"nce1c69039c7f47f0","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":true,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In step 3's inventory add tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py and replace its hard-coded `version=\"3.6.1\"` arguments (L193, L247) — and the fake_convert `pandoc_version=\"3.6.1\"` / expected `\"version\": \"3.6.1\"` literals (L103/L111) — with the new bundled version or `generator.LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION`; extend step 7 verification to run `pytest tests/scripts/test_generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_a